
== §88 — TEST J: COORDINATION DIFF ON A MEP-ADJACENT WALL ==
  ✓ the MEP-adjacent wall move previews
  ✓ coordination runs on the base model
  ✓ coordination runs on the candidate model
  ✓ the three declared diff classes are computable
  ✓ the classes are exactly the ones the specification declares
  ✓ every finding is accounted for in exactly one class
  ✓ the MEP model is not touched by the architectural edit
  ✓ no MEP element was rerouted
  ✓ no coordination finding was auto-resolved by the engine
  ✓ the specification forbids auto-fix in its own words
  ✓ a preview never reports a coordination change as a blocking error

== §53/§55 — POLICY DISTINGUISHES INTEGRITY FROM COORDINATION ==
  ✓ a model-integrity failure is an ERROR
  ✓ a coordination change is only a WARNING
  ✓ a navigation change is only a WARNING
  ✓ stale derived data is merely INFO
  ✓ not all coordination changes are blocked outright
  ✓ warnings still require an explicit acknowledgement by default

== §56 — NAVIGATION IMPACT IS FACTUAL, NOT A JUDGEMENT ==
  ✓ deleting a door previews
  ✓ the runtime portal count actually changes
  ✓ the connectivity graph is recomputed from the candidate
  ✓ a lost connection is reportable as a fact
  ✓ the connectivity report makes no compliance judgement
  ✓ the dependency graph marks navigation stale for a door delete
  ✓ no navigation result claims a code outcome

== §57/§58 — EGRESS AND DISTANCE STAY NOT_EVALUATED ==
  ✓ egress is marked stale by a door delete
  ✓ distance is marked stale by a geometry change
  ✓ the specification keeps compliance NOT_EVALUATED for these
  ✓ no authoring result carries a PASS or FAIL verdict
  ✓ a committed geometry change reports the transaction compliance as NOT_EVALUATED
  ✓ a geometric distance may be recomputed on the candidate without a rule comparison
  ✓ no rule result is carried forward across the change

== §59/§60/§61 — STRUCTURE, MEP AND FLS ARE NEVER MUTATED ==
  ✓ MOVE_WALL: no structural column, beam or foundation is moved by the engine
  ✓ MOVE_WALL: no duct, pipe or cable is rerouted by the engine
  ✓ MOVE_WALL: no fire or life-safety record is retargeted by the engine
  ✓ MOVE_WALL: the dependency report states no discipline was mutated
